{
 "slug": "baikal",
 "lines": [
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "This one lake beats all five Great Lakes.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS *ONE LAKE*",
    "BEATS ALL|*FIVE* GREAT LAKES."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "How does it beat all five, if it's barely bigger than Belgium?",
   "chunks": [
    "HOW DOES IT|BEAT *ALL FIVE,*",
    "IF IT'S BARELY|BIGGER THAN *BELGIUM?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Meet Lake Baikal, in Siberia. The Great Lakes are not impressed.",
   "chunks": [
    "MEET LAKE *BAIKAL,*",
    "IN *SIBERIA.*",
    "THE GREAT LAKES|ARE *NOT IMPRESSED.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "We're almost eight times bigger!",
   "chunks": [
    "WE'RE ALMOST|*EIGHT TIMES* BIGGER!"
   ],
   "speaker": "superior"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "On a map? Sure. So where is Baikal hiding all that water?",
   "chunks": [
    "ON A MAP? *SURE.*",
    "SO WHERE IS BAIKAL|*HIDING*",
    "ALL THAT *WATER?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Straight down.",
   "chunks": [
    "STRAIGHT *DOWN.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Baikal plunges 1,642 metres. About four times deeper than Lake Superior.",
   "chunks": [
    "BAIKAL PLUNGES|*1,642 METRES.*",
    "ABOUT *FOUR TIMES* DEEPER",
    "THAN LAKE *SUPERIOR.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Nobody asked you to measure.",
   "chunks": [
    "NOBODY ASKED YOU|TO *MEASURE.*"
   ],
   "speaker": "superior"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "That's nearly five Eiffel Towers deep.",
   "chunks": [
    "THAT'S NEARLY",
    "*FIVE EIFFEL TOWERS* DEEP."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "But why so deep? Baikal isn't sitting in a valley. It's filling a crack in the Earth.",
   "chunks": [
    "BUT WHY|*SO DEEP?*",
    "BAIKAL ISN'T SITTING|IN A *VALLEY.*",
    "IT'S FILLING|A *CRACK*",
    "IN THE *EARTH.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Right here, the ground is slowly pulling apart.",
   "chunks": [
    "RIGHT HERE,|THE GROUND",
    "IS SLOWLY|*PULLING APART.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "That crack opened 25 to 30 million years ago. Which makes Baikal the oldest lake on Earth.",
   "chunks": [
    "THAT CRACK OPENED",
    "*25 TO 30 MILLION*|YEARS AGO.",
    "WHICH MAKES BAIKAL",
    "THE *OLDEST LAKE*|ON EARTH."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "The Great Lakes? They filled up about 14,000 years ago.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE *GREAT LAKES?*",
    "THEY FILLED UP|ABOUT *14,000* YEARS AGO."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Can we change the topic?",
   "chunks": [
    "CAN WE CHANGE|THE *TOPIC?*"
   ],
   "speaker": "superior"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "And the crack is still opening. About four millimetres, every year.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND THE CRACK",
    "IS *STILL OPENING.*",
    "ABOUT *FOUR MILLIMETRES,*|EVERY YEAR."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Width makes a lake look big. Depth makes it big.",
   "chunks": [
    "*WIDTH* MAKES A LAKE|LOOK BIG.",
    "*DEPTH* MAKES|IT BIG."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Here's the twist. The water isn't even the bottom.",
   "chunks": [
    "HERE'S THE *TWIST.*",
    "THE WATER ISN'T EVEN|THE *BOTTOM.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Below the lake floor lies up to seven kilometres of mud. The crack goes down about as far as Everest is tall.",
   "chunks": [
    "BELOW THE LAKE FLOOR",
    "LIES UP TO|*SEVEN KILOMETRES* OF MUD.",
    "THE CRACK GOES DOWN",
    "ABOUT AS FAR AS|*EVEREST* IS TALL."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "And from above? It still looks barely bigger than Belgium.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND FROM *ABOVE?*",
    "IT STILL LOOKS|BARELY BIGGER THAN *BELGIUM.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Why do I keep getting dragged into this?",
   "chunks": [
    "WHY DO I KEEP",
    "GETTING *DRAGGED*|INTO THIS?"
   ],
   "speaker": "belgium"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "This is BHUGOL. Follow for more Geography Fun Facts.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS IS *BHUGOL.*",
    "FOLLOW FOR MORE|GEOGRAPHY FUN FACTS."
   ]
  }
 ],
